{"name":"Tuscan Wall","hex":"#fcc492","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wall","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rampart of earth, stones etc. built up for defensive purposes.","A structure built for defense surrounding a city, castle etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enclose with, or as if with, a wall or walls.","To use a wallhack."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wall","blocks":[{"text":"A wall is a structure and a surface that defines an area; carries a load; provides security, shelter, or soundproofing; or serves a decorative purpose. There are various types of walls, including border barriers between countries, brick walls, defensive walls in fortifications, and retaining walls that hold back dirt, stone, water, or noise. Walls can also be found in buildings, where they support roofs, floors, and ceilings, enclose spaces, and provide shelter and security."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Noel_2005_P%C3%A9kin_031_muraille_de_chine_Mutianyu.jpg/330px-Noel_2005_P%C3%A9kin_031_muraille_de_chine_Mutianyu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wall","wikidata":"Q42948"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/J.L._Gerome_-_The_Wailing_Wall_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-J.L._Gerome_-_The_Wailing_Wall_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/J.L._Gerome_-_The_Wailing_Wall_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-J.L._Gerome_-_The_Wailing_Wall_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/J.L._Gerome_-_The_Wailing_Wall_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-J.L._Gerome_-_The_Wailing_Wall_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=e